# Process: verify_medication_invoice_compatible
#
# Objective:
# Verify that an invoiced medication is approved for a specific patient.
# This version intentionally uses parser-supported patterns.

# Load payload document context
Load document

# Extract core fields from invoice payload text
Find patient id and save as patient_id
Find medication name and save as medication_name
Find ndc code and save as ndc_code
Find quantity and save as invoice_quantity
Find refill count and save as invoice_refill_count
Find service date and save as service_date

# Initialize decision state
manual_review equals false
decision_status equals pending

# Required data checks (single-line conditionals)
manual_review equals true if patient_id == nil
decision_status equals needs_review if patient_id == nil

# Medication eligibility checks
# Note: service lookups are represented as extract/search placeholders for now.
Find approved medication list and save as approved_list
Find normalized medication and save as normalized_medication

manual_review equals true if approved_list == nil
decision_status equals needs_review if approved_list == nil
manual_review equals true if normalized_medication == nil
decision_status equals needs_review if normalized_medication == nil

# If a normalized medication is found and list exists, attempt deterministic path
# Current parser does not support block-style if/otherwise statements yet.
# We stage values and enforce numeric guards below.

Find quantity limit and save as quantity_limit
Find refill limit and save as refill_limit

# Conservative defaults if values are absent are handled in gateway pre-processing.
invoice_quantity must be at most 30
invoice_refill_count must be at most 3

# Confidence threshold (percentage encoded as integer)
Find mapping confidence and save as mapping_confidence
mapping_confidence must be at least 90

# Routing hooks
Send notification to payment integrity team if manual_review == true
Email billing team if decision_status == approved
